- core/stats/glm.py: glm_analysis — binomial (logit, probit, cloglog;
  trials column or constant m) and Poisson (log) GLMs by maximum
  likelihood (statsmodels IRLS); explanatory component from an optional
  block (fitted first, intra-block analysis), up to two treatment factors
  and a transformed covariate:
  - analysis of deviance with χ² or, with estimated dispersion, deviance
    ratios and F (Tables 18.2–18.4, 18.6, 18.11);
  - over-dispersion test against χ²(ResDF), deviance or Pearson estimate
    of φ, φ̂ < 1 not used, binary data flagged (18.2.2, 18.2.7);
  - sequential analyses of deviance in both factor orders (Table 18.7);
  - first-level-zero parameters with SE·√φ, z or t (Table 18.8);
  - predictions per cell (Table 18.9), averaged before and after
    back-transformation with back-transformed CIs (Example 18.2E),
    covariate predictions and fitted curve on the original scale;
  - level differences with ratios (log) or odds ratios (logit)
    (Example 18.3C); standardized deviance residuals.
- Tests against Tables 18.3, 18.6–18.9, 18.11 and Examples 18.1B–D,
  18.2B, 18.2E, 18.3B–C (Tables 18.1, 18.5, 18.10, 18.12 data added).
- Catalog (trials slot), i18n, bridge, messages.

